  "difficulty_level": "H2",
  "difficulty_reason": "Matlis duality exchanges all Artinian and Noetherian modules over a complete local Noetherian ring, including modules that are not finite length. Its retained proof core reconstructs the completion as the endomorphism ring of the injective hull, derives the hull descending-chain condition from Noetherian completion, and builds finite injective copresentations from finite socles and essential torsion embeddings before transporting presentations through an exact contravariant functor. This completion/injective-hull structural duality is substantially beyond finite-dimensional vector-space duality or ordinary qualifications.",
